  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Light to occasionally moderate rain is likely \nlate Wednesday into Thursday with an isolated thunderstorm \npossible in the North Thursday afternoon. Little to no drought \nrelief expected.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nLow pressure stalling out to our northwest will result in\nshowery and unsettled weather over the area, especially the\nNorth, beginning early this afternoon. Rain overspreads much of\nthe area overnight tonight with a band of moderate rain moving\nthrough the Bangor and Downeast region early Thursday morning.\nAs the cold front of the low passes to our north Thursday\nafternoon, current guidance is showing the potential for some\nconvection along it over the North. Model soundings show some\nweak instability up to 500 J/kg which could produce some\nthunder. Low freezing levels around 7500 ft may favor some small\nhail with any storms. Overall, not expecting any severe storms.\nThe potential for drought relief is relatively low as total \nprecipitation is expected to be generally below 0.25 inches with\nthe highest amounts over the North.",
